Now test. Reload mobile page. Use run-code to start, set player near veil, orient, set scanHeld true, wait 5s, check. Need compute yaw/pitch. We can position player at e.g., (veil.x, veil.y+2, veil.z+20) and look at veil. The scan target requires distance < range and alignment. Use helper in eval:
```
const v = h.creatures.veil.scanPosition;
h.player.position.set(v.x, v.y+3, v.z+22);
const dx=v.x-h.player.position.x, dy=v.y-h.player.position.y, dz=v.z-h.player.position.z;
const horiz=Math.hypot(dx,dz);
h.player.yaw=Math.atan2(-dx, -dz); // forward = (-sin yaw, ..., -cos yaw), so -sin yaw=dx/horiz => sin yaw=-dx/horiz => yaw=atan2(-dx,-dz)
h.player.pitch=Math.atan2(dy,horiz);
h.input.scanHeld=true;
```
Wait 5s, check. But rAF may be slow. Use `await page.waitForTimeout(5000)` and eval. Let's do.

