content.text:
Update comments maybe. Need `world.update` uses dt .1 but scan progress uses raw up to .25. Good.

Start pointerdown and maybe title tap. Add:
```
startButton.addEventListener('pointerdown', (event)=>{ if(event.pointerType==='touch') startGame(); });
```
But click also. For desktop pointerdown first triggers start before click; fine. But Playwright click uses pointerdown -> startGame immediately; click then ignored. Good. Could add all pointer types. Be careful: `startGame` calls `audio.start()` on pointerdown user gesture. Good. Add `startButton.addEventListener('pointerdown', startGame);` before click. Might fire twice but guard. Also handle `mouseenter`? no.

Also title-screen tap on coarse? We can optionally add `titleScreen.addEventListener('pointerdown', ... )` only if isCoarse and target is not button? But pointerdown on whole title could start when dragging? On title there's no drag functionality. Nice. However mobile user might tap to see title? It's already shown for 300ms. Tapping anywhere starts. "TAP TO DIVE" aligns. Let's add:
```
if (isCoarse) {
 titleScreen.addEventListener('pointerdown', (event) => {
   if (event.target.closest('button, a')) return;
   startGame();
 });
}
```
But startButton itself triggers too. Fine. Could conflict with sound? title has no sound. Good. But if user taps the title "HALOVALE" starts, expected.

Maybe for desktop add click anywhere? no.

Add `document.body.classList.add('touch')` maybe for CSS? not needed.

Update start note in HTML `−13 M`. Also maybe title says "DIVE LOG 07 · −13 M". Let's.

Update favicon in index head.

CSS edits.

